# Lecture 09H

## Ordered Tetrads and Centromeres

## Chapter 8

## Dr. Neil Voss

## November 3, 2026

=== layout: bookend

# Learning Objectives

@body

- Follow meiosis and mitosis to form eight ordered spores.
- Classify first- and second-division segregation.
- Explain the half-weight and calculate gene-to-centromere distance.

=== layout: definitions

# Ordered Tetrad Terms

@body

- [*Spore (Ascospore)*]{color=#24578F}: a haploid reproductive cell; here, one of eight cells inside an ascus.
- [*Ascus*]{color=#24578F}: the sac that holds the ordered spores.
- [*First-Division Segregation (FDS)*]{color=#076DAD}: alleles separate at meiosis I, giving a 4:4 pattern.
- [*Second-Division Segregation (SDS)*]{color=#B74300}: alleles separate at meiosis II, giving 2:2:2:2 or 2:4:2.

