=== layout: reference

# Ordered Tetrad Mapping Reference

@body

{table-style=comparison}
| Segregation | Ordered Eight-Spore Pattern | Use in the Numerator? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| First division (FDS) | 4:4 | No |
| Second division (SDS) | 2:2:2:2 or 2:4:2 | Yes, with half weight |

- SDS is a count of whole asci; N includes both FDS and SDS.
- One crossover involves two of four chromatids, so take half the SDS count.

$$
D = \frac{\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{SDS}}{N} \times 100 \;\mathrm{cM}
$$

@citation

Gene-to-centromere estimate using the single-crossover model; multiple crossovers are neglected.

